assistant: Subject: Accept epoch-millisecond created_at in get_order

Vendor API version 2026-10-01 sends `created_at` as a number of epoch milliseconds (e.g. `1792142857943`) instead of the ISO-8601 string in the published spec. `get_order` ran every value through `Date.parse(String(...))`. A number-string like that doesn't parse, so the code fell back to `|| 0` and returned `1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z`. The fix: when `created_at` is a number, use it directly as milliseconds; strings are still parsed the old way, so v1 output is unchanged. typecheck, lint and tests all pass. The `|| 0` fallback is still there, so a value that can't be parsed in some future format would again show 1970 instead of failing visibly. I left it alone to keep this change small.

